


FILL IN DATA STRUCTURE NEEDED FOR OBSERVATIONS


save observations into a csv file and place in run/observations

the csv file should contain the following column headers:

'azimuth', 'date', 'days', 'elevation', 'error_var', 'height', 'index', 'kind', 'lat', 'lon', 'seconds', 'utime', 'value', 'x', 'y', 'z'


note that error_var will get overwritten in computeHx.py. 

azimuth is in degrees with 0 to the north
date is in datetime format
elevation is in meters
kind is observation type: 11 = VR, 12 = DBZ, 13 = DBZ0, 14=DBZ0_W (see namelist readme for info on what these variables are)